# A SUPPLIED TEST IMAGE for whole minion_tlb (B11).
#
# NOT hardware initialization provenance: these are chosen test values, and the
# driver reports the state as supplied-from-file either way.
#
# The TLB cache RF is aw 3, dw 69.  Every word is (1 << 60) + address, which
# FITS 69 bits, so `setWord`'s `mk_bv 69` normalisation leaves it unchanged --
# an earlier version of this file used a 128-bit word 0 and 2^70..2^76 for the
# rest, which `mk_bv 69` silently reduced to [2^69-1, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0].
# That file is retained as a preflight negative.
#
# Every word differs from the source-derived expectation 0x223600abcde ABOVE
# BIT 31, so a committed write cannot be confused with the initial contents and
# a gate that only reaches the low lanes cannot produce it.
memstate v1
flops reset
mem 3 69 295147905179352826879
word 0 1152921504606846976
word 1 1152921504606846977
word 2 1152921504606846978
word 3 1152921504606846979
word 4 1152921504606846980
word 5 1152921504606846981
word 6 1152921504606846982
word 7 1152921504606846983
